WEBVTT

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:35.920
It's cold.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.290
I wonder what's taking so long.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:09.880
Hello.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:10.910
H-Hey.
Hello.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:11.740
Oh, hi.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.320
It's been a while, Kugayama-san.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:17.300
Well, graduation is n-next week,

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.910
so I c-came to pick up my personal belongings.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.560
I-I'm having second thoughts about taking them back, though.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:29.650
I guess that's why stuff piles up each year.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:30.510
M-Maybe.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.840
Kugayama-san, you were employed by
a medical equipment manufacturer, right?

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.500
Yeah. It's more of an apparatus manufacturer, though.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.160
D-Do you want to see their catalog?

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.480
Oh, I see.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.720
This kind of thing, huh?

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:50.610
I-It's a small company,
b-but when I went to t-training the other day,

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:54.950
I-I had the feeling that I'd
be stationed at s-sales.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.970
Oh, man. Kugayama-san's in a pinch.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.080
Hey.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.050
Hello.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:00.810
Hey.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:01.530
Hello.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.200
Please don't change jobs on a whim.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.570
Wh-Why'd you say that?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.870
Isn't it common for people to
quit after a short tenure these days?

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.640
Oh, are you guys talking about the upcoming spring?

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.640
W-Well, the office is located in Iidabashi,

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.960
s-so I don't think I'll quit since the location's really convenient.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.090
The main factor is the location, huh?

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.060
T-Tanaka, you'll be in Ueno, right?

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.960
The school itself? Yeah.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.310
Y-You'll be close to Akiba, won't you?

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:31.110
Well, Nippori would be better as far as I'm concerned.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:35.240
Nippori has a lot of places that
sell garments and sundries, after all.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.030
Right.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.930
Is that...

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.550
It's not that I can't commute from my apartment,

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.530
but it's a fairly long distance.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.790
You're going to move, aren't you?

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.650
Why wouldn't he? It won't be too far away, anyway.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:54.900
It isn't a problem.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.630
Come on. I already explained it to you.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:01.040
As I said earlier, that's fine with me.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.140
Don't say it like that.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:03.550
Listen to me.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.700
I'm sorry.
Listen to me.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.140
You don't have to apologize.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.570
Hey.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.920
Kousasa isn't here yet?

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:12.490
Saki-san!

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.300
I need to ask you for a small favor, Saki-san.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.110
What is it?

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.520
Since Tanaka-san will be graduating next week,

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.920
the costumes he's made for you have piled up over the months.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:33.100
That's why I was thinking about holding an
all-out photo session to commemorate the graduation.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:33.630
What do you think?

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.930
I'm not the one who's graduating, am I?

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.370
Are you serious?

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:51.230
What do you say?

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:53.440
Well, let's see...

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.540
Commemoration, huh?

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.450
Oh, how about next year?

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:03.490
Let's do everything at the same time when we graduate.

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:07.680
I'll be able to do it to the fullest extent.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.660
I don't think I'll be able to do that this year.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:10.620
It'll be the year after that.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.580
I'm a transfer student...

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.160
I can only graduate the year after next at
the earliest because I don't have enough credits.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.020
Everyone will graduate before me!

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.560
Don't be silly.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.540
We still have an entire year left.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.610
How are you going to get through it like this?

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:50.090
When I graduate,
I'll make sure I cosplay until you're completely satisfied.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:55.340
Even after you graduate, please come to the Comifes.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.260
Well, it's not like I go there very often.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.520
<i>Graduation, huh?</i>

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:11.580
<i>President?</i>

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.040
<i>Vice President!</i>

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.210
<i>Congratulations.</i>

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:44.110
As I conclude this speech,
I pray for your success in the future. Congratulations.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:52.510
Oh, you're graduating?

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:54.730
It might become a little more
peaceful around here from now on.

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:56.940
I made sure to prepare my underclassmen.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:04.000
<i>Why are you disbanding our club without prior warning?</i>

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.010
<i>What did you say, you otaku?</i>

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:07.630
<i>I'm not an otaku!</i>

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:16.310
<i>Is that okay with you?
I saw it through
the opening of the student council door.</i>

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:21.520
<i>The itching must be unbearable during the summer.</i>

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:27.690
I assume you're going to start a career after graduation.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.610
Aim for an executive seat.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:32.680
No, you might make a better entrepreneur.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:35.830
Do I have that kind of image?

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:37.120
Without a doubt.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:40.340
Unfortunately for you,
I don't plan on working.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:41.840
I'm going to marry soon.

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.430
Marry? Are you talking about that guy?

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:51.100
<i>You could get infected from the doormat.</i>

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:52.720
<i>It's okay!</i>

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.420
Don't refer to him as that guy.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.150
Congratulations.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:08:59.510
Thanks.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:00.690
<i>But...</i>

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.920
Yeah, you were right. It's him.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.040
He's a year older than I am,
so he's already been working.

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:13.160
I appreciate all the trouble you went through just to set us up.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.580
See you later!

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:16.540
Hey...

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.200
W-What about your athlete's foot?

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.090
Dammit.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:29.790
Why do I feel like I've completely lost from a woman's perspective?

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:31.830
What is it?

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:33.650
Nothing.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:38.270
Well, I didn't expect it to become adapted three times.

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:42.070
I would have preferred if they aired
everything simultaneously in one series.

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:43.680
I'm sure there was some demand for it.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:50.730
The fact that it's become an OVA says a lot
about the unsettling situation of the Kujiun anime.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.970
Personally, I'm just glad they released it.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:58.320
They also kept the ending for the first part exactly the same.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.920
I-I'm surprised Koike Koutarou took the offer.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:05.530
More so since he wasn't involved in moe anime before then.

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:08.670
I heard he fell in love with the first series.

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:10.220
S-Seriously?

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:15.140
Yeah. He had studio connections with Director Mizudori.

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:18.520
He graced us with the skills of a veteran.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:23.910
It was similar to the original plot, but the scenes
that made you laugh and cry were handled better.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:30.290
He assembled all of the characters and ended it with
some drama between the president and vice president.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.670
It really hit my soft spot.

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:36.280
Th-The f-first series really did live up to expectations,

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:44.700
c-considering they were forced to c-change the
ending from the manga due to time constraints.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.280
Remember when they had to
postpone the show because of the typhoon?

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:49.710
The director of both series fled.

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:53.340
P-People flamed the scriptwriter on his blog.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.300
A lot of things happened.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:58.930
W-Well, I think it was a fortunate twist of fate.

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:01.840
As they say, everything becomes nostalgic in the end.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:11.850
Well, the series was over as far as I was
concerned when the president left to study abroad.

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.100
What do you mean by over?

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.530
I was talking about Kujiun.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.110
Otaku talk, even during an occasion like this?

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.780
Well, the end of the story was recently released as an OVA.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.060
Who cares?

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:28.340
Pictures! Let's take some pictures.

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:29.900
You, too, Saki-chan.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:32.530
I don't want to.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:33.960
Don't act like a child.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.600
I'll take it.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:40.060
Hey, where's Madarame?

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:40.900
Please don't move.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.450
He said he'd be here.

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:45.630
That aside, did he find a job?

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:50.660
Whenever I ask him,
he mumbles a vague answer, so I can't really tell.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.640
Sasahara-senpai, stand still.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:56.180
Is he going to remain unemployed
and find himself wandering around?

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.240
Saki-san!

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.500
The probability of that is pretty high.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:02.000
Stop moving around!

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:05.210
Understood?

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:06.470
Yes, sir!
Yes.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.080
I'm going to take it.

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:10.750
Sorry guys.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.550
It's about time. How's the job hunt going?

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:16.210
How's it going?

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:19.260
Ogiue-san, please take a picture.

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:20.700
Ogiue-san? Ogiue-san?

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:23.900
Are you still undecided?

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:23.920
Ogiue-san? Ogiue-san?

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:24.660
Who knows?

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:24.830
Ogiue-san!

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:26.580
That doesn't sound very reassuring.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.060
Ogichin, this way.
Ogiue-san?

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:32.550
We still have some time before the farewell party.

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.450
I'd like to change.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:38.150
Let's meet up in the club room in a little bit.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.090
What about my pictures?

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:42.490
Oh, Madarame.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:45.330
Oh, Yana, is the Manga Club also hosting a farewell party?

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.210
Yeah, I think so.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:49.650
C-Congratulations on your graduation.

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:53.600
I saw Iroha Gokko.
There was some reaction from our female members.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.040
One of jealousy, of course.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.900
I think it was the right move to put you in Genshiken.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.850
I don't regret making the request.

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:02.470
Thank you.

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:05.710
By the way, did you hear about Haraguuro?

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:07.440
What happened?

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:09.470
He's at odds with
Kazamatsuri Neko-san right now.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:13.040
It looks like Haraguuro sold
some of his works without permission,

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:16.600
threatening to charge a price between 500.000 and 1 million yen for each one.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.710
Wow, one million.

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:23.830
Kazamatsuri-san instantly became famous when it was known that he was working on the key frames of Nouvelle Vague.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:27.680
Haraguuro's been in hiding for the past month or so.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.640
Serves him right.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.720
You might be right.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.960
By the way, Sasahara,

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:38.800
Yes?

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.890
are you still going to serve as president?

00:13:40.890 --> 00:13:43.430
Are you not going to resign as a senior?

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:45.230
Oh, president, huh?

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:47.060
Well, to be honest,

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.760
I was going to ask Ohno-san to take over.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.560
Oh.

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:53.650
I was going to abdicate the presidency to Ohno-san.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:55.670
N-N-N-No way!

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:58.230
I can't be the president!

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:03.780
Well, still,

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:05.700
you know...

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:08.960
Well, if you're busy, I understand.

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:10.670
I'm not doing anything.

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.410
It's not that I'm busy, but...

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:15.230
Kasukabe-san, give her a few words of encouragement.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:16.840
Why me?

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.800
It's become a club tradition.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:19.760
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:23.890
Why don't you accept the presidency
and change it to a cosplay research club?

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.350
I'll do it!

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:31.610
Oh, no.

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:34.060
Are you sure you don't want to take that back?

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.150
Was that a mistake?

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:38.350
Saki-san, let's start with your cosplay...

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.310
I said I'd do it at the end.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:51.020
Oh, she ran away.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:52.820
She's chasing after her.

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:55.360
O-Ohno-san seems all right.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.210
Well, somewhat.

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:59.300
Cheers!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.700
Great job, everyone!

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:05.010
Not at all.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:07.230
Excuse me. Another beer, please.

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:09.260
<i>That was quick!</i>

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:15.480
Why don't we start a Genshiken reminiscence meeting?

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:17.900
Let's start with your fondest memories.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:27.110
Let's see. How could I not mention...

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:29.910
Kasukabe-san's cosplay!

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:54.610
Those are my memories, not yours!

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:56.060
They're the worst kinds of memories, too!

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:57.810
They're not bad at all.

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:01.730
We managed to catch the voyeur
in the act, which was a good thing.

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:05.400
Voyeur? Qu'est-ce que c'est?

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:10.250
It's the legendary tale of Kasukabe-san,

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:13.260
the story of a Ritsuko Kübel Kettenkrad look-alike contest.

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.290
Don't say another word!

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:17.910
It's really something I want to forget about.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:18.960
One more beer please!

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:22.910
Now, now. Kasukabe-san, you still have another year left.

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:26.880
There's plenty of time for you to
make more wonderful memories.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.550
I don't want to hear that from you!

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:29.890
Is that so?

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.190
What do you think? Take a look.

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:38.730
Wow, that's something!

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:40.270
<i>He didn't have to bring it here.</i>

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:42.950
Well, it's far from finished.

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:44.540
The details are pretty rough right now.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:46.900
It doesn't look like it's your first attempt at all.

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:51.240
What's with you, showing it off like that?

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.860
That's sexual harassment, you know!

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:57.380
He added the details on the lingerie by using me as a model.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:16:59.790
You didn't have to say that.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:02.630
Ohno, do you wear that kind of underwear?

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.660
Of course I don't!

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:08.010
It's about details, you know, details!

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:09.470
Another beer!

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:11.060
Huh? Seriously?

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:13.180
Well, it was only for reference.

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:16.350
Let me see it! Let me see it!

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:19.160
I don't think you should trust Kasukabe-san.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.680
<i>Are you supposed to move it
by holding the joints?</i>

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:22.350
<i>Yeah, that's ri—</i>

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:28.710
That was an accident.
I mean, I wasn't sure about what I was doing in the past.

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:30.960
I promise I won't break it.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.700
Actually, you should break it, Saki-san.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:37.620
Pretend it was an accident.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:39.240
See?

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:45.620
It looks kind of creepy since it's completely gray.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.220
Aren't you going to paint it?

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:48.170
<i>Wow.</i>

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.890
<i>That's cutting it close.</i>

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:53.890
<i>Speaking of which, Ogiue-san, too.</i>

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:55.290
<i>Today seems to be...</i>

00:17:57.980 --> 00:17:59.850
S-Sorry, can I have it back?

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:01.230
Here you go.

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:03.260
You had me sweating.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:05.450
I-Isn't it detachable?

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:07.900
I don't know how to do it.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:20.750
That wasn't my fault, was it?

00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:25.660
It's divine punishment!

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:30.840
If I had known this was going to happen,
it would have been easier on me if Kasukabe-san did it.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.170
Why is everyone talking about me?

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:39.160
W-Well, Kasukabe-san was
Genshiken's main attraction.

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:40.430
Don't say it in past tense!

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:44.840
Yes, I still remember Nee-san's and Kousaka-senpai's—

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:45.870
Don't say another word.

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:47.270
...kiss.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:47.980
Shut up!

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.600
I don't even know whose farewell party this is for anymore.

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:55.970
Find a job. Find a job, okay?

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:59.820
Do it for the sake of both your parents
back at home and for your own well-being.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:02.490
Whether it's a part-time job or something else, just find work!

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:07.010
Oh, yeah. Well, it's been taken care of for the time being.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:09.610
Really?

00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:10.550
For the time being.

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:11.830
Which is it?

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.090
Yeah, it's been decided.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:14.770
Where? Where?

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:15.770
W-Where?

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:22.270
Sakura Pipe Construction. It's a company that
conducts sanitation maintenance for water-related stuff.

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:24.320
Will you dig?

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:25.890
Where will you be working?

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:27.110
I'll only be doing clerical work.

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:28.440
I won't have to go outside.

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:30.610
In Tokyo or back home?

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:35.580
Well, about ten minutes
by foot in this direction.

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:36.410
I think.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:40.900
What the hell's up with that?

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:42.200
That's really close.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.120
It's the same as it is now.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:46.710
I think I saw a billboard for it.

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:48.040
Are you going to frequent the campus?

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.390
No way, idiot!

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:53.760
I'm going to be an office worker.
I won't have time to visit the university.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:58.720
Yeah, I know a few people who still live near the campus.

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:02.230
Well, the rent around here is pretty cheap.

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:05.680
You won't be able to grow up that way.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:06.390
Shut up!

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:09.270
Well, at least you found a job.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:12.150
I received a compliment.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:15.400
Thank you very much.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.620
It's over.

00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:20.640
I-It's still pretty c-cold.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.700
It still feels like winter during the night.

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:26.750
Shall we do an ipponjime?

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:28.190
How about three banzai cheers?

00:20:28.190 --> 00:20:31.020
L-Let's not. I-It doesn't fit our image.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:31.980
You're right.

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:33.740
Let's just go home.

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:34.870
How boring.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:36.950
See you later.

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:38.690
There won't be a later, you know.

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:39.800
Well, you'll only be ten minutes away.

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:41.310
I have to catch my train!

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:43.050
We have to hurry.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.340
What a mess.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.100
Oh, it's snowing.

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.450
You're right.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:53.420
Good job, guys.

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.030
Good job.

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:06.790
<i>Kugayama Mitsunori,</i>

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:09.720
<i>Tanaka Souichirou,</i>

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:12.630
<i>Madarame Harunobu.</i>

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:17.550
<i>Those three individuals finally graduated today.</i>

00:22:51.530 --> 00:22:53.100
Hey.

00:22:53.420 --> 00:22:55.270
Hey.

00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:01.320
Is something wrong?

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:02.030
Is it my suit?

00:23:03.010 --> 00:23:04.850
I feel so tired all of a sudden.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:09.170
Why?

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:13.750
What is eroticism for an otaku?

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:16.050
I-Isn't it all about illustrations?

00:23:16.050 --> 00:23:19.910
There are occasions when we
inadvertently think that crude drawings are moe,

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:23.130
since we respond by saying,
"This might turn out well. Look at these unrefined sketches."

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:25.230
It depends on the situation or the plot.

00:23:25.230 --> 00:23:27.560
It could be school swimsuits,
extreme sadism, or huge breasts.

00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:31.080
It could also be specific fetishes like ribs and collar bones.

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:36.210
Oh, much like how a fujoshi fulfills the
stereotype,
we basically think everything is moe.

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:39.350
Hey, he summarized everything.
